ocracy that  brought that about  do you think if there is a commission or  anything congress does to look into  january 6 at this point will be  looked at as credible if you're going to  enact policies to make sure this never  happens again as the  independent bipartisan september 11  commission did  it has to be independent bipartisan and  as far  away from this building as possible mike  is there anything that  any questions you have from one six that  haven't been answered i'm done like  tiptoeing through the tulips here  the questions i have are you know to  what extent if any did  uh are political leaders involve  themselves in the events of  january 6th if there was uh  participation from  members of congress from their staff as  an officer that served that day  i certainly would like to know that like  as an american i believe very strongly  in a in a  two-party system um  right now one of those parties has a  cancer  and we gotta cut it out and until we do  that we're not gonna be able to move  forward as a nation  cbs news is not aware of any evidence  that indicates a member of congress  aided the rioters on january 6th nearly  500 people  have been charged and the fbi says  hundreds more  may soon be facing charges as well  officer fanon has been a regular  presence up here on the hill trying to  meet with members of congress that have  been minimizing what happened on january  6.  last week he says a house republican  member refused to even shake his hand  and he has been unable to get a meeting  with house minority leader kevin  mccarthy  mccarthy's office says the leader is  happy to meet with vanone  but has not received an official meeting  request  anthony chris thank you that's that's  pretty astonishing and  what's also astonishing is every time we  see another angle uh or another  body camera from from this assault on  january 6 it it just looks scarier and  scarier every time  yeah an independent bipartisan  commission i'm interested in what they  would find but also what they will not  find as chris mentioned there's no  evidence someone in congress  cooperated in any way with the rioters  let's put that in a report if that's  what the investigators find  i think the scariest thing in all of  this an investigation is not going to  change the minds and hearts of people  who think  that wasn't a big deal yeah i don't  understand when your house is attacked  as  congress was you don't agree to an  investigation first breach in over 200  years  yep

